{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins","id":1068146,"title":"MtAw: Mage Assassins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-25T19:37:25-07:00","id":1068146,"title":"MtAw: Mage Assassins","content":"Understanding that the focus of Mage stories tends to follow the theme of mystery and investigation more than combat, there are still a broad range of constructs that focus on combat.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, there must be an example of a Legacy designed to quietly assassinate the enemies of the orders. <br /> <br /> I've found a broad range of stealth legacies, but none of them overtly describe themselves as assassins.<br /> <br /> Have I missed something, or is that by direct design?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T20:01:38-07:00","id":1068154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrKorpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins#post1068146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understanding that the focus of Mage stories tends to follow the theme of mystery and investigation more than combat, there are still a broad range of constructs that focus on combat.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, there must be an example of a Legacy designed to quietly assassinate the enemies of the orders.<br /> <br /> I've found a broad range of stealth legacies, but none of them overtly describe themselves as assassins.<br /> <br /> Have I missed something, or is that by direct design?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that generally, any Legacy purely based off of killing is going to be branded as Left Handed. Sure, you can have stealthy Legacies based around gathering information, or snooping into things they probably shouldn't, and people of those Legacies might even have to kill on occasion. But to shape your soul into a tool used purely to kill others (even those deemed enemies) is going a bit too far. I honestly don't think that any Order other than the Seers would condone such a thing.<br /> <br /> Edit: Not to say they don't exist because they almost certainly do, but this isn't the type of thing the Orders would really talk about and let spread around. They'd likely treat you as a potential Banisher, and while they might not kill you for it outright, it's something you'd almost certainly want to keep hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-25-2017, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T20:05:11-07:00","id":1068155,"title":"","content":"Thread Cutters are the go-to legacy for assassination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T20:17:25-07:00","id":1068158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068154#post1068154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that generally, any Legacy purely based off of killing is going to be branded as Left Handed. Sure, you can have stealthy Legacies based around gathering information, or snooping into things they probably shouldn't, and people of those Legacies might even have to kill on occasion. But to shape your soul into a tool used purely to kill others (even those deemed enemies) is going a bit too far. I honestly don't think that any Order other than the Seers would condone such a thing.<br /> <br /> Edit: Not to say they don't exist because they almost certainly do, but this isn't the type of thing the Orders would really talk about and let spread around. They'd likely treat you as a potential Banisher, and while they might not kill you for it outright, it's something you'd almost certainly want to keep hidden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points! I had considered that angle as well. Wisdom (as designed in 1.0) doesn't like killing outside of self-defense.<br /> <br /> Separate from the concept of violence, I think the Princes of Many Masks are a very interesting spy concept...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T21:49:41-07:00","id":1068175,"title":"","content":"Chun of Shinanju: &quot;Assassination is the highest form of public service.&quot;<br /> Chun may not have been a Mage but the Guardians would definitely agree with this sentiment and they are all about tarnishing their own souls to protect others and no, they wouldn't talk about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T23:52:55-07:00","id":1068203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrKorpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins#post1068146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understanding that the focus of Mage stories tends to follow the theme of mystery and investigation more than combat, there are still a broad range of constructs that focus on combat.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, there must be an example of a Legacy designed to <b>quietly assassinate the enemies of the orders</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the job of the Guardians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T01:50:56-07:00","id":1068221,"title":"","content":"Legacy attainment use can't be an Acts of Hubris.<br /> So a Legacy of assassins who only used their legacy attainments would have disturbingly high Wisdom for a cult of killers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T04:05:37-07:00","id":1068234,"title":"","content":"As was mentioned the Thread Cutters, a GV Legacy, are the &quot;Assassins&quot; as they will kill to enforce someones Fate upon them. Even though they are not all about Assassinations they are labeled as Left-Handed by some, not all, mages for their willingness to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T04:24:53-07:00","id":1068239,"title":"","content":"Seems odd to me that the Arrows would not find the idea of killing your enemy to be perfectly acceptable, and have Legacies based on that.<br /> <br /> Not like Perfected Adepts can't and don't just use their attainments to develop awesome physical power which they then apply by shoving their fists through the skulls of their enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T04:34:10-07:00","id":1068241,"title":"","content":"There is a difference in killing someone in combat and assassinating them. The Legacy of the Thread Cutters is developed around killing to accomplish the goals of the Legacy, the Perfected Adept isn't. There are some Arrows out there the probably feel the way that you do but I don't know of any Legacy that the arrows follow that prescribe to assassination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:19:39-07:00","id":1068253,"title":"","content":"Adaptability is Strength, though, and Assassination is a strategy of war. A very effective one at times, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T07:51:00-07:00","id":1068291,"title":"","content":"Just for the sake of discussion, I imagine the angle of confrontation in Mage is kind of like the dynamic between Batman and the Joker...<br /> <br /> \u200bIn other words, the 'good guy' (the PC) doesn't kill the 'bad guy' because it's a strong imperative in the Code of Conduct. And on the flip side, the 'bad guy' doesn't directly act to kill the 'good guy' because life would be so empty without the challenge. It's an odd balance of (often twisted or seemingly illogical) logic.<br /> <br /> Plus: if the PC's can assassinate their targets without too much issue, then so can the enemy... and do we want to open that door?<br /> <br /> \u200bStill... one of the many angles of a character's story arc can be that of the falling protagonist (the anti-hero), with the question being: Will the PC come back to Wisdom, find an uncomfortable balance of good and evil within themselves, or fall utterly into Hubris and madness? Playing a character that - within certain defined boundaries - performs the role of an occasional assassin might create that storyline nicely. The point of that, of course, is the story being told... not the body count.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:28:15-07:00","id":1068303,"title":"","content":"Well there could be several reasons a single mage or even a small group of mages might become assassins, but a legacy on the whole would at the very least be frowned upon the the mage society as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:32:31-07:00","id":1068305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrKorpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068291#post1068291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the sake of discussion, I imagine the angle of confrontation in Mage is kind of like the dynamic between Batman and the Joker...<br /> <br /> \u200bIn other words, the 'good guy' (the PC) doesn't kill the 'bad guy' because it's a strong imperative in the Code of Conduct. And on the flip side, the 'bad guy' doesn't directly act to kill the 'good guy' because life would be so empty without the challenge. It's an odd balance of (often twisted or seemingly illogical) logic.<br /> <br /> Plus: if the PC's can assassinate their targets without too much issue, then so can the enemy... and do we want to open that door?<br /> <br /> \u200bStill... one of the many angles of a character's story arc can be that of the falling protagonist (the anti-hero), with the question being: Will the PC come back to Wisdom, find an uncomfortable balance of good and evil within themselves, or fall utterly into Hubris and madness? Playing a character that - within certain defined boundaries - performs the role of an occasional assassin might create that storyline nicely. The point of that, of course, is the story being told... not the body count.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very PG approach to the World of Darkness. How do your players respond to that?<br /> I feel like the WoD is about choices and consequences, and no choice carries greater consequences than deciding to end someone's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T09:28:24-07:00","id":1068326,"title":"","content":"Boston Unveiled has a 300-year-old cabal called the Gravediggers who have acted as assassins on behalf of the Consilium. They are currently mostly Arrow.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure a legacy about that could exist in the Arrow. But I think it would be rare simply because devoting and remolding your soul to killing people is unnecessary and the legacy would more likely about something else and killing people would just be how they go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T10:09:54-07:00","id":1068331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068253#post1068253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adaptability is Strength, though, and Assassination is a strategy of war. A very effective one at times, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that this takes it to a degree higher than mage society would probably be comfortable with. Again, this isn't some minor thing you're doing. You are making a statement. You permanently shape your soul/Gnosis into a tool designed solely for the act of murder. It isn't some possible worst case scenario use here, you are changing the deepest most sacred part of yourself into a that of a perfect killer. What does that say about you as a person that you fixate your life purely around ending the lives of others? <br /> <br /> Again, there are Legacies that probably have a high body count, but they typically aren't designed for that purpose alone. I really see such a Legacy being little more than a breeding ground for Banishers and Reapers. Letting them kill to their hearts content, free of any inherent magical consequence. Again, the only Orders I see permitting such a thing are the Seers and probably the Guardians, and even then I see them being <i>at</i> <i>best</i> borderline Left-Handed, not spoken of, and rarely trusted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T10:23:30-07:00","id":1068335,"title":"","content":"The problem with Legacy making is that you need to make sure that the thing you are shaping your soul into is...well...worth shaping your soul into.<br /> As far as legacies go, I currently reaaaaaaaaaallllllllllly want to write up a Legacy (though note that this would be probably a single-person Legacy; we aim at &quot;Legacies are reflection of a individual person&quot; and want to use them in order to emphasize individuals, not create magical mini-orders) with Time and Death, focused around destroying objects and killing people while sending them to the past, in order to prevent greater sin and damage. Very Guardian/Arrow. <br /> Users Wisdom would be untouched, because each time they judge someone guilty and execute the punishment, Mage in question kinda commits a temporal suicide by collapsing the current timeline and rewritting everything due to evildoers death - all the blame and sin of killing is placed upon the Time Killer who disappears along with the killed timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-26-2017, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T15:35:33-07:00","id":1068444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068326#post1068326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... But I think it would be rare simply because devoting and remolding your soul to killing people is unnecessary and the legacy would more likely about something else and killing people would just be how they go about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Souls devoteed into Killing&quot; is never unnecessary when the act can make you insane and a Legacy Attainment can solve this. Also, being a Pentacle mage does not make you saint. A vengeful Pentacle mage that lost family members would join such a Legacy out of spite. I think there are enough reasons to become Obsessed with murder in a World of Darkness even without including insane lunatics.<br /> <br /> Generic Assassin Legacy Mechanics (thus far)<br /> Order: Mostly Banishers, Nameless. Seers and Left-handed. but prized informaly even by Pentalce Consilia under situations were murder seems the only option. Arrow/Guardian for Pentacle<br /> Initiation: Voluntarily killing a Sleeper, Sleepwalker or Mage using magic<br /> Attainments: Direct Damaging Spells, Harmfull Conditions, setting up fatal narrative effects, Unmaking Magick. Powers that help mundane assassination<br /> <br /> But how do you roleplay <b>a High Wisdom Legacy Assassin </b>(that is NOT in Adamantine Arrow or Guardians of the Veil)?<br /> If said person regularly abuses the Attainment &quot;just for the lols&quot; with no apparent reason, would he still retain his High Wisdom?<br /> How does he percieve the<b> difference between</b> murder by<b> mortal means</b>, murder by <b>Innured Spell </b>and murder by <b>Legacy Attainment</b>, is there any at all?<br /> <br /> It seems to me that the worldview of such a person would be far from what we conceive as &quot;human&quot; even with High Wisdom. And a profound way of why Awakened are monsters (despite being &quot;sane&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","user":"Shadowjim12","date":". 03-26-2017, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T15:35:59-07:00","id":1068445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrKorpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068291#post1068291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bStill... one of the many angles of a character's story arc can be that of the falling protagonist (the anti-hero), with the question being: Will the PC come back to Wisdom, find an uncomfortable balance of good and evil within themselves, or fall utterly into Hubris and madness? Playing a character that - within certain defined boundaries - performs the role of an occasional assassin might create that storyline nicely. The point of that, of course, is the story being told... not the body count.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that angle of a story arc can only work if the assassination are NOT done by using Legacy Attainments. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12644_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12644\" data-vbnamecard=\"12644\">HerbertIsBestBert</a> said, using a Legacy Attainment is never an Act of Hubris. No Wisdom risk, much less loss.<br /> To add to this, it can also not work if the player uses Inured spells to carry out the assassinations.<br /> <br /> The story arc you describe is that of just being a member of the Adamantine Arrow, or the Guardians of the Veil. These folk may, at times, be required to take someone out. And not neccessarily in the heat of battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back to the core topic!<br /> <br /> Having an assassination-focused Legacy is a Bad Idea for the mages entering it. Secrets only stay secret for so long in the Awakened society. And I don't doubt it would be declared Left Handed very quickly.<br /> <br /> Not to say it wouldn't be an interesting story. You could play out the story of Yagami Light of Death Note. (off the top of my head, Death Note is an Artifact, Ryuk is a spirit of death and a low-dot Mentor as he doesn't do overly much other than nomnom on essence in form of apples)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:09:42-07:00","id":1068453,"title":"","content":"If you want Hubris-free killing tools, you can just Inure yourself to the spell that does the deed. Which also makes you rely on that spell to do the deed. Which also means that you are going to forge a killing pattern. Which means that it can be identified and tracked. Which means story potential and fixing of one of the most annoying things that plagued previous edition of the Mage, &quot;having no reason to stick to certain solutions instead of doing it differently each time to make sure you never form a weakness&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T18:07:54-07:00","id":1068497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068445#post1068445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having an assassination-focused Legacy is a Bad Idea for the mages entering it. Secrets only stay secret for so long in the Awakened society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're a Logophage and you've dedicated your life to the assassination of Truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T18:11:15-07:00","id":1068499,"title":"","content":"I want a Logophage legacy updated to fit the 2nd Ed PRIME EQUALS TRUTH paradigm. I loved Logophages.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> I wanted to say &quot;DEATH TO MIND AS LOGOPHAGE ARCANUM&quot;, but then I remembered that you can develop unorthodox attainments for your Legacies, so I'm suddenly excited about &quot;Mind+Death&quot; Logophages, &quot;Prime+Death&quot; brand of Logophages, and &quot;Prime+Mind&quot; brand of Logophages. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-26-2017, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T18:16:09-07:00","id":1068500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068499#post1068499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to say &quot;DEATH TO MIND AS LOGOPHAGE ARCANUM&quot;, but then I remembered that you can develop unorthodox attainments for your Legacies, so I'm suddenly excited about &quot;Mind+Death&quot; Logophages, &quot;Prime+Death&quot; brand of Logophages, and &quot;Prime+Mind&quot; brand of Logophages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a Moros legacy with Prime ruling now. Should be pretty sweet if it ever gets updated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T18:23:13-07:00","id":1068501,"title":"","content":"One thing I really like about the way the new Legacy system works (minus the &quot;unorthodox attainment is one gnosis harder, sorry&quot;), is that I can take ideological cores of the Legacies...and allow players to develop their own Attainments around these concepts using their own pairs of Arcana. Why? Because really good Legacies tend to stand on their own two feet even when you remove their Arcana from them - you could do Eleventh Question using pretty much any pair of the Arcana, because it's core concept allows so much flexibility and space. <br /> Eleventh Question is great, it poses a question, and while you can use the corebooks answer to it, it's written in a way that allows you to pick what you believe is your own answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T18:52:20-07:00","id":1068506,"title":"","content":"We know there are in fact assassins among the Guardians thanks to the Moros write-up for Mayfly, the late life Awakening and assassin who worries about his children finding out.<br /> \u200bAs for shaping your soul for the sole purpose of murder? You wouldn't have to. Legacies provide Attainments from two Arcanum and multiple times, all that is required is that one of those Attainments be useful for murder while the others could provide more personal benefits (not to mention helping cover up the murder).<br /> \u200bAssassins aren't serial killers and they aren't terrorists, they kill a specific person for a cause, a cause that at least for a time comforts them that they are doing right and blinds them to arguments against. Later, after fatigue and disappointment set in, they often question their activities but by then it is far too late for their victims.<br /> \u200bBanishers would unavoidably find their way to such Legacies. For them magic is murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T19:42:29-07:00","id":1068515,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of presumption that the magic entwined in the Legacy Attainments is the direct tool for assassination, rather than for the tools to put you in the position to accomplish the assassination and help cover up the work.<br /> <br /> <i>Princes of Many Masks </i>and <i>Subtle Ones</i>\u200b are two legacies that provide pretty darn good attainments for someone who might want to do some spying as a primary duty, with some assassinations on the side now and again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T19:49:44-07:00","id":1068518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrKorpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068515#post1068515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of presumption that the magic entwined in the Legacy Attainments is the direct tool for assassination, rather than for the tools to put you in the position to accomplish the assassination and help cover up the work.<br /> <br /> <i>Princes of Many Masks </i>and <i>Subtle Ones</i>\u200b are two legacies that provide pretty darn good attainments for someone who might want to do some spying as a primary duty, with some assassinations on the side now and again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because the original post asked about Legacies designed for the purpose of assassination, not for Legacies designed for other things that could, on the side, be used by assassins. There's a huge difference in there being a Legacy that could be used by assassins and one designed with the intent to help you be a better assassin. Reality Stalkers are great spies and infiltrators and would make pretty damn good assassins if used for that end, but that isn't their <i>purpose</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T21:34:05-07:00","id":1068542,"title":"","content":"It seems like Interfectors would benefit from such a legacy. They're executioners by definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T02:49:44-07:00","id":1068589,"title":"","content":"Although Interfectors aren't assassins, they're executioners. So that's a different thing as well.<br /> <br /> An assassin Legacy for me would be all about using, I dunno, Death, Time and Space to cover up your tracks. Maybe you have no sympathetic links with the victim at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T03:14:10-07:00","id":1068592,"title":"","content":"Time and Space to find the victim, isolate the victim and completely cover up the deed, the body and the sympathetic connections that was created.<br /> I think an Acanthus legacy with Space as Ruling Arcanum and Time as optional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T04:26:15-07:00","id":1069243,"title":"","content":"I think an assasin legacy would be ok as long as it isn't about killing people for killings sake.<br /> You could make a legacy of assasins that studies the mysteries that arises from the consequences of the assasination. The attainments could be time, space and fate focused both to help in the deed and more importantly studying the consequences. Like arsons staying at the scene of the crime to watch the fire and the consequences of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T05:18:09-07:00","id":1069259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068506#post1068506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assassins aren't serial killers</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, &quot;assassin&quot; is pretty much defined as a kind of serial killer. There's a notable number assassins in real world history who were even sociopathic serial killers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and they aren't terrorists, they kill a specific person for a cause, </div> </div> </div> Killing people for a cause is pretty much a modern definition of terrorist, as used in American society today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T06:02:13-07:00","id":1069275,"title":"","content":"'sup :&gt;<br /> <br /> An executioner kills because it's his duty, a bounty hunter\\assassin do it for something in exchange, a serial killer do it for his own psychic issues, terrorists have a terror agenda and causes enforced by homicides.<br /> <br /> Ritual killing should be a serial killer thing, in the Fallen World at least.<br /> <br /> I think Excecutioners would be the most acceptable form of murderer for the pentacle, while both them and terrorists would be loved by the Exarcs.<br /> Exarcs would kinda like ritual killers too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T06:48:55-07:00","id":1069298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Bardiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1069275#post1069275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">terrorists would be loved by the Exarcs.<br /> Exarcs would kinda like ritual killers too</div> </div> </div> </div>The FC engages in terrorism, especially the Blank Badges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T07:10:38-07:00","id":1069316,"title":"","content":"Real life: There is this story I've heard repeated about the Vietnam war, about a volunteering recruit that when asked why he volunteered in his examine he frankly answered &quot;Because I want to kill people&quot;. He was not allowed to join. (And for good reason, people willing to kill are not the same as people with the active desire to kill)<br /> <br /> I think we can draw anologies to Awakened conflict. Assasin is a word dripping with religious fanaticism and allegations of drug use to alter the mind to make people killers in its origins.<br /> <br /> Normal people and by extension normal Mages are usually only comfortable with the idea of assassins in fiction, and if the topic was more real would kick in instictual red flags in the back of the mind because such beings are not safe nor stable. (And with breaking points acting as a barrier to most beings against horrific violence, those able to kill without that barrier become legitimately more dangerous than those who'd suffer a breaking point because the cost violence is cheaper for them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-28-2017, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T08:40:02-07:00","id":1069378,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Teamwork Spellcasting Rolls.<br /> <br /> Can I use them with instant spell rolls? Or just with Ritual Spellcasting?<br /> I don't see anything that specifically calls for Ritual Spellcasting only, so I just want to be sure about this.<br /> <br /> Cause Egregore will be way more powerfull with this.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Sorry, wrong topic &gt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> I was reading this and trying to post on Ask a Question topic.<br /> I'll leave the question on a spoiler just for giggles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 03-28-2017, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T11:32:15-07:00","id":1069501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1069259#post1069259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, &quot;assassin&quot; is pretty much defined as a kind of serial killer. There's a notable number assassins in real world history who were even sociopathic serial killers.<br /> <br /> Killing people for a cause is pretty much a modern definition of terrorist, as used in American society today.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By any real world definition, an assassin would be definable as potentially mentally ill. But this isn't the real world. It's the World of Darkness.<br /> With that in mind, there are reasonable mindsets that allow for a rational support of the stealthy killing of another human being. The majority of said applications are, of course, military... covert operations. I don't imagine any of us would casually refer to the Navy Seals (for example) as terrorists or insane sociopaths, yet they are often put in a position to snipe a target, sabotage enemy installations, or even perform silent kills with a knife during sensitive black ops missions. It's nasty business, but some are willing to put themselves in that position - <i>not because they enjoy it</i> - but because doing such things reduces risk and prevents greater losses of life.<br /> <br /> When I first posted the concept, I had no intention of implying that it would be a celebration of murder and violence. If there was such a Legacy, it would have to be based very strongly in the concept of Duty and Self-Sacrifice. And there'd be Much prep work done to ensure the potential new member possesses the psychological wherewithal to withstand the stresses of such a position without going nuts...<br /> <br /> And, of course, the average mage is an academic... not a soldier. But this is a frightening world filled with all manner of potential opposition that won't resort to simple curses and petty thefts to ruin your day. Angry spirits, vengeful ghosts, goetic manifestations, Acamoth... all wait to rip a mages world apart. And that not even including the other systems. Lycanthropes aren't exactly known for their subtle applications of what they think is justice. Vampires, while very subtle, also often have no problem with the idea of hunting down and killing your entire family if necessary... for the next ten generations. Demons, constructs, and who knows what else?<br /> <br /> Mages would have a military (and they certainly do in the form of the Arrow), and every military has its covert specialists. And if quietly killing the insane leader of a twisted cult of corrupted terrorists causes the rest of said organization to fall apart with minimal bloodshed, why would a sane person choose to engage in a direct frontal assault that would result in the bloody deaths of large numbers of people? And maybe with the leader gone, some of the followers can be saved and returned to sanity/Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Like I said... it wouldn't be about a body count. It would be the opposite.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","user":"DrKorpal","date":". 03-28-2017, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T12:31:45-07:00","id":1069541,"title":"","content":"My biggest issue with an assassin Legacy is the same one I have with Legacies as a whole, if you are going to shape your soul which Legacy would you choose?<br /> \u200bI don't know if Legacies and their Attainments are supposed to carry on after death but if you are shaping your soul do you choose a form that is convenient now, or seek some higher and eternal form?<br /> \u200bIf Legacies are only about mortal life than maybe picking one with Attainments that make your 9 to 5 easier makes sense, but what about later in life when you're no longer doing that job and realize something else would serve you better now? You can't change your mind later, at least not without a difficult Astral Journey.<br /> \u200bMeta game thinking makes it easy, &quot;Of course I pick the power that makes killing Orcs easier, that's the only part of this character's life I'm going to play after all&quot;, but if you think about it in character the ability to shoot a fly at fifty paces isn't worth much if you only fire a gun a dozen times in your life.<br /> \u200bSome Legacies make sense to me (Eyes of Ain Soph; Mages are obsessed with mysteries) but others feel like when they ask a kid what superpower he would pick and he says invisibility so he can sneak into the girl's showers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T13:12:11-07:00","id":1069565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1069541#post1069541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue with an assassin Legacy is the same one I have with Legacies as a whole, if you are going to shape your soul which Legacy would you choose?<br /> \u200bI don't know if Legacies and their Attainments are supposed to carry on after death but if you are shaping your soul do you choose a form that is convenient now, or seek some higher and eternal form?<br /> \u200bIf Legacies are only about mortal life than maybe picking one with Attainments that make your 9 to 5 easier makes sense, but what about later in life when you're no longer doing that job and realize something else would serve you better now? You can't change your mind later, at least not without a difficult Astral Journey.<br /> \u200bMeta game thinking makes it easy, &amp;quot;Of course I pick the power that makes killing Orcs easier, that's the only part of this character's life I'm going to play after all&amp;quot;, but if you think about it in character the ability to shoot a fly at fifty paces isn't worth much if you only fire a gun a dozen times in your life.<br /> \u200bSome Legacies make sense to me (Eyes of Ain Soph; Mages are obsessed with mysteries) but others feel like when they ask a kid what superpower he would pick and he says invisibility so he can sneak into the girl's showers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter because throwing yourself fully into your legacy can cause you to ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T18:51:50-07:00","id":1069769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1069541#post1069541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue with an assassin Legacy is the same one I have with Legacies as a whole, if you are going to shape your soul which Legacy would you choose?<br /> \u200bI don't know if Legacies and their Attainments are supposed to carry on after death but if you are shaping your soul do you choose a form that is convenient now, or seek some higher and eternal form?<br /> \u200bIf Legacies are only about mortal life than maybe picking one with Attainments that make your 9 to 5 easier makes sense, but what about later in life when you're no longer doing that job and realize something else would serve you better now? You can't change your mind later, at least not without a difficult Astral Journey.<br /> \u200bMeta game thinking makes it easy, &quot;Of course I pick the power that makes killing Orcs easier, that's the only part of this character's life I'm going to play after all&quot;, but if you think about it in character the ability to shoot a fly at fifty paces isn't worth much if you only fire a gun a dozen times in your life.<br /> \u200bSome Legacies make sense to me (Eyes of Ain Soph; Mages are obsessed with mysteries) but others feel like when they ask a kid what superpower he would pick and he says invisibility so he can sneak into the girl's showers.</div> </div> </div> </div>well the killing should be a mean, not the end. mages are already _quite_ good at ending lives.<br /> and attainments should not be related to the killing, but to the supernal scope<br /> <br /> imho, the legacy should have flavour without being too much cheesy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T19:59:28-07:00","id":1069804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrKorpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1069501#post1069501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By any real world definition, an assassin would be definable as potentially mentally ill. But this isn't the real world. It's the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, its the Chronicles of Darkness, not World.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, of course, the average mage is an academic... not a soldier. </div> </div> </div> Not exactly true. The average mage is going to be engaged in a war with the Seers at minimum. Its one of the three major themes of the game - The World Is a Lie paragraphs involve talking about fighting the Seers and Exarchs in pretty much the entire length. So, while you can say that a magei sn't a carrer soldier, they are expected to be fighters and warriors. And there's the question about if non-Mysterium are actually academics either. So, should the average mage be considered an academic in the first place? I don't think that argument has weight to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-28-2017, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T20:40:59-07:00","id":1069834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1069804#post1069804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The World Is a Lie paragraphs involve talking about fighting the Seers and Exarchs in pretty much the entire length.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Not really? It talks about how the Exarchs are oppressive in the opening lines, sure, but the Seers aren't mentioned at all and the general tenor of response to the Lie that's alluded to is more in the vein of <i>escape</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T14:00:20-07:00","id":1070283,"title":"","content":"The great thing about the system is that everyone here is right...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T22:48:31-07:00","id":1071077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068146-mtaw-mage-assassins?p=1068589#post1068589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although Interfectors aren't assassins, they're executioners. So that's a different thing as well.<br /> <br /> An assassin Legacy for me would be all about using, I dunno, Death, Time and Space to cover up your tracks. Maybe you have no sympathetic links with the victim at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like the idea of a legacy that gets to know a target intimately in a short span of time. (using Space and Time, probably) When the assassin finally truly understands the subject, he can use an attainment to sever their connection, removing all lesser ties and their ties to life and body in one fell stroke. That could be a fun take.<br /> Could link it by legend to the <i>Emperor and the Assassin</i> tale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}